# Ruric Thar, Magecrusher's "Ruric Thar has hexproof as long as they haven't dealt combat damage yet" (CR 702.11,
# 604.1, 611.3a). Before any combat damage, Bot2's Unsummon cannot target it, while the same Unsummon targeting Bot2's
# own Ornithopter works (the positive control). Bot1's own Giant Growth does target it, hexproof stopping only opponents.
# On turn three it attacks with vigilance (untapped) and trample: the Ornithopter blocks for two and the other eight go to
# Bot2, so it has dealt combat damage. On turn six the second Unsummon now targets it
# and returns it to Bot1's hand. Bot1 recasts it on turn seven: a new object (CR 400.7) has dealt no combat damage, so it
# has hexproof again and Bot2's third Unsummon on turn eight is refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Ruric Thar, Magecrusher
Giant Growth
Black Lotus
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
